{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0187V47EXYU5oVbHCxH9DTZT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully and propose the next task.\n\n## Step 1: Analyze Project Context\n\nThis is a project called go-unix-utils that:\n- Derives formal specs from C source code of Unix utilities\n- Generates Go implementations from those specs using AI\n- Verifies parity against reference binaries through differential testing\n\n## Step 2: Summarize Project State\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations diverge in behavior. This project uses spec-driven development to generate Go implementations and verify them against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**:\n- `cmd/` - Per-utility Go implementations\n\n\n- `pkg/testutils/` - Differential testing harness\n- `pkg/sys/` - Syscall abstractions (Darwin/Linux)\n- `pkg/format/` - Output formatting\n- `magefiles/` - Build targets\n- `docs/` - Specifications, PRDs, use cases, test suites\n\n**Current State**:\n- `pkg/testutils` - spec complete, code exists (difftest.go, normalize.go)\n- `pkg/sys` - spec complete, no code yet\n- `pkg/format` - spec complete, no code yet\n- `cmd/ts` - spec in progress (PRD complete, use case documentation started)\n- Other utilities - specs in various stages, no implementations\n\n**Current Release**: rel01.0 (in_progress) - ts specification and differential test\n\nFor rel01.0, the critical path is finishing the `cmd/ts` implementation since the PRD and use case documentation are already done, along with the test suite. The differential testing harness in `pkg/testutils/` is ready to support this work.\n\nLooking at the dependencies, `cmd/ts` only needs the standard Go time libraries and the existing test utilities—no other packages are required. Given the constraint of one task and the priority to implement before testing, I should focus on building the ts utility itself. Let me check what the PRD specifies for the core requirements.\n\nThe implementation covers R1 through R8: default timestamp behavior, custom format strings, incremental mode, elapsed-since-start mode, monotonic clock mode, relative-time conversion, error handling, and environment variables. R9 is purely about differential testing, so that's separate. I'm counting up the sub-requirements to understand the scope of work needed. I need to handle strftime format string conversion since Go's time package uses a different formatting syntax than the standard strftime that ts expects.\n\nThe task should cover flag parsing, reading stdin line-by-line, converting strftime formats to Go's time format, supporting subsecond extensions, and implementing the various modes like incremental, elapsed, monotonic clock, and relative time conversion—all with proper error handling and timezone support. This is manageable within the expected scope for a utility described as trivial.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":73725,"cache_read_input_tokens":18565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":73725},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"325dab79-4127-4556-8835-8b60056067db","uuid":"94be736f-175e-4ac5-ba54-5f66c124af59"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0187V47EXYU5oVbHCxH9DTZT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that derives formal specs from C/Perl source of Unix utilities, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: `cmd/` holds per-utility Go binaries, `pkg/testutils/` provides the differential testing harness, `pkg/sys/` wraps platform-divergent syscalls, `pkg/format/` handles shared output formatting, and `magefiles/` exposes build targets.\n\n**Current state**:\n- `pkg/testutils/` — code exists (`difftest.go`, `normalize.go`), harness operational\n- `cmd/ts` — PRD complete (prd004-ts), use case written, test suite written, **implementation pending**\n- `pkg/sys/`, `pkg/format/` — specs complete, no code yet\n- All other utilities — specs in various stages, no implementations\n\n**Current release**: rel01.0 (in_progress) — single use case `rel01.0-uc001-ts` (in_progress). The ts implementation is the blocking deliverable.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nrel01.0 is the earliest incomplete release. Its sole use case (`rel01.0-uc001-ts`) requires a working `cmd/ts` binary and differential tests. Per the dependency map, ts needs only `pkg/testutils` (already implemented) and Go standard library — no `pkg/sys` or `pkg/format`. Per P2, implementation and tests are split into separate tasks. Per P8, implementation comes before tests. The next task is implementing `cmd/ts/main.go`.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/ts implementation: prd004-ts R1-R8 timestamp stdin lines\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd004-ts.yaml (full PRD for ts -- all requirements R1-R8)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.0-uc001-ts.yaml (use case flow and success criteria)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.0.yaml (test cases that this implementation must satisfy)\n      - docs/specs/sources.yaml (ts source is Perl, flag parsing at ts:64, flags -r -i -s -m)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests -- the harness this binary will be tested against)\n      - pkg/testutils/normalize.go (TimestampNormalizer -- understand what normalization tests will apply)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ts/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Complete ts utility implementation: flag parsing, stdin timestamping, all modes (-i, -s, -m, -r), strftime format support including subsecond extensions, exit codes, TZ handling\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Default behavior (prd004-ts R1.1-R1.6): Read stdin line by line, prepend timestamp in default format \\\"%b %d %H:%M:%S\\\" evaluated at line-receive time, flush after each line, preserve original newlines, handle partial last lines (no trailing newline), exit 0 on EOF, suppress SIGPIPE.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Custom format string (prd004-ts R2.1-R2.4): Accept optional positional argument as strftime format string. Support standard strftime(3) conversion specifications by converting them to Go time.Format layout strings. Support three ts-specific subsecond extensions: %.S (seconds with 6-digit microsecond suffix e.g. \\\"32.001234\\\"), %.s (Unix epoch with 6-digit microsecond suffix e.g. \\\"1708358732.001234\\\"), %.T (HH:MM:SS with 6-digit microsecond suffix e.g. \\\"14:05:32.001234\\\"). Obtain second and microsecond from a single time.Now() call per line.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Incremental mode -i (prd004-ts R3.1-R3.4): Timestamp shows elapsed time since previous line was received. First line shows elapsed since ts started. Default format \\\"%H:%M:%S\\\" with TZ=GMT internally. Custom format overrides the default but TZ=GMT still applies. -i and -s are mutually exclusive -- print usage error to stderr and exit non-zero if both given.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Elapsed-since-start mode -s (prd004-ts R4.1-R4.3): Timestamp shows elapsed time since ts started, increasing monotonically across lines. Default format \\\"%H:%M:%S\\\" with TZ=GMT internally. Custom format overrides the default.\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Monotonic clock mode -m (prd004-ts R5.1-R5.3): Use Go time.Now() monotonic reading for timestamp sampling. Compatible with all format modes and custom format strings including subsecond extensions. Timestamp must not jump on wall-clock adjustments.\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Relative-time conversion mode -r (prd004-ts R6.1-R6.5): Scan each input line for known timestamp patterns (syslog \\\"Jan  5 14:30:00\\\", ISO-8601 \\\"2024-01-05T14:30:00.000Z\\\", RFC 2822 with optional day \\\"16 Jun 94 07:29:35 GMT\\\", lastlog \\\"Mon Jan  5 14:30\\\") and replace with human-readable relative age string (e.g. \\\"15m5s ago\\\"). When -r and a format string are both given, convert matched timestamps to the specified format via strftime. Lines with no recognized timestamp pass through unchanged. -r is mutually exclusive with -i and -s.\"\n      - id: R7\n        text: \"Exit codes and error handling (prd004-ts R7.1-R7.3): Exit 0 on clean EOF. Exit non-zero with usage message to stderr for unrecognized flags. Document that the Go implementation compiles in all parsing support (the Date::Parse unavailability condition from R7.3 cannot arise).\"\n      - id: R8\n        text: \"Environment handling (prd004-ts R8.1-R8.2): Respect TZ environment variable for wall-clock timestamps in default mode. In -i and -s modes, use TZ=GMT internally for elapsed-time formatting regardless of user TZ setting.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Strftime-to-Go conversion: Implement a strftimeToGo(format string) function that maps strftime directives (%Y, %m, %d, %H, %M, %S, %b, %B, %a, %A, %p, %Z, %z, %j, %u, %w, %s, %T, %F, %R, %n, %t, %%) to Go reference-time layout tokens. Pre-process the ts-specific extensions (%.S, %.s, %.T) by replacing them with sentinel placeholders before conversion, then substitute the actual microsecond values after time.Format() returns.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Elapsed time formatting for -i and -s modes: Compute the delta as a time.Duration, convert to seconds, construct a time.Time from epoch + delta seconds, then format with TZ set to time.FixedZone(\\\"GMT\\\", 0). This matches the Perl source behavior where TZ=GMT causes strftime on a delta-second value to produce correct elapsed strings.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Flag parsing: Use the Go standard library flag package. Define -i, -s, -m, -r as boolean flags. The remaining non-flag argument (if any) is the custom format string. Validate mutual exclusivity (-i/-s, -r/-i, -r/-s) before entering the main loop. Print usage to stderr and os.Exit(1) on validation failure.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Relative time patterns for -r mode: Compile regexp patterns matching the four timestamp formats from prd004-ts R6.2 (syslog, ISO-8601, RFC 2822, lastlog). For each match, parse into time.Time, compute time.Since(), and format as a relative age string using the largest two non-zero units (e.g. \\\"2h15m ago\\\", \\\"3d5h ago\\\", \\\"45s ago\\\").\"\n      - id: D5\n        text: \"SIGPIPE handling: Call signal.Notify for syscall.SIGPIPE and start a goroutine that calls os.Exit(0) on receipt, matching GNU behavior where SIGPIPE terminates silently. This is simpler than importing pkg/sys (which ts does not need per dependency-map.yaml).\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/ts/main.go compiles with `go build ./cmd/ts/` with no errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"echo 'hello world' | go run ./cmd/ts produces a line matching the pattern \\\"<Mon> <DD> <HH:MM:SS> hello world\\\" (prd004-ts AC1).\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"printf 'a\\\\nb\\\\nc\\\\n' | go run ./cmd/ts -s produces three lines with monotonically increasing elapsed timestamps in HH:MM:SS format (prd004-ts AC2).\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go run ./cmd/ts with an invalid flag (e.g. -z) prints a usage message to stderr and exits non-zero (prd004-ts AC4).\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Empty stdin (no input, immediate EOF) produces no output and exits 0 (prd004-ts AC5).\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go run ./cmd/ts -i -s prints a mutual-exclusivity error to stderr and exits non-zero (prd004-ts R3.4).\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"printf 'no timestamp here\\\\n' | go run ./cmd/ts -r passes through the line unchanged (prd004-ts R6.4).\"\n      - id: AC8\n        text: \"The produced binary runs under golangci-lint with no warnings (prd004-ts AC6). Run: golangci-lint run ./cmd/ts/...\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":73725,"cache_read_input_tokens":18565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":73725},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"325dab79-4127-4556-8835-8b60056067db","uuid":"8a82ccd3-84ee-4e9b-9045-604c36ac5401"}
